in this video we'll talk about positron  emission tomography scan  or  pet scan  now pet scan is a technique that reveals  the metabolic or biochemical function of  your tissues and organ  in this technique the key player is the  positron  which is the antimatter counterpart of  the electron in this video we'll talk  about  mechanism of pet scan  use of pet scan to detect cancer and  other underlying pathological situations  interpretation of the pit scan data  by the way this video was made in  collaboration with the nerd medic  youtube channel  don't forget to follow the channel and  subscribe it  i believe you have heard of different  imaging modalities like ct scan and mri  but why we need another imaging modality  such as pet  basically pet scan  is a functional imaging whereas mri and  ct scan both are structural imaging that  means mri and ct scan gives you a  glimpse of the structural or anatomical  organization of different  organs or tissues  whereas the pet scan gives you a  functional imaging that means it shows  the level of functioning or extent of  functioning of those tissues  now we will learn how pet scan is  performed  now  the pet scan machine is kept in a  separate radiation proof room  in the machine  there's a scanner and in that machine  the patient lies down and the patient is  put into the machine tunnel  in a separate room the operator sits  with a computer where the scan  results are  seen  now as i told you this pet scan uses  radiation and that that's why this has  to be kept in a radiation proof room  now let us understand what biology plays  behind the principles of pet scan  now we all know that human body has  different tissues  like brain and liver  whose metabolic activity require glucose  now glucose  forms atp by different metabolic  pathways and this atp is known as the  energy currency of the cell this energy  currency supplies energy for different  metabolic and cellular activities  now this glucose is present in our  bloodstream whenever the cells require  this glucose they take up the glucose  from the blood  now  now this principle was exploited by the  scientists  to develop a scanning technique such as  pet  so they developed a molecule known as 18  fdg or 18  fluorodeoxyglucose which is a glucose  analog  which emits positrons the antimatter  analog of electron  now let's learn more about 18 fdg  now 18 fpg when injected into the blood  competes with glucose  for getting uptaken in the cells using  similar mechanism  now when cells uptake the 18 fdg 18 ftg  emits positrons now these positrons come  in contact with the electrons that are  already present in different molecules  of the cell  and electron is a matter positron is the  antimatter counterpart of electron so  matter antimatter when they come  together in close contact they undergo a  reaction known as annihilation reaction  now this annihilation reaction gives  rise to gamma rays which  go out  in equal and opposite direction  these gamma rays are picked up by the  scanner or the detector  and the two gamma rays moving in exactly  opposite direction picked up at the same  point of time  is known as the coincidence imaging so  this is the core physics principle  behind the pet scan that is coincidence  imaging  now  there can be two situations now in one  situation  where we have highly metabolically  active  cells  they will take up a lot of glucose and  as they take up a lot of glucose their  fdg intake will also be high and hence  they will  emit a lot of gamma rays because  more more amount of fdg will ensure more  amount of annihilation reaction and from  that we will get more amount of gamma  emission  on the other hand in situation 2 we have  less metabolically active cells they  will take up less amount of glucose  similarly they will take up less amount  of fdg less amount of fdg means less  amount of positron less amount of  positron means less amount of  annihilation reaction so gamma the  emission will be low  now based on these principles let us  interpret the pet scan data  now in situation 1 where we have gamma  emission high  we can see in the image that will give  you a high or dense signal this is known  as a hot spot  whereas when metabolic activity is low  gamma emission is low that gives rise to  a low signal a low density signal known  as a cold spot this hot spot and cold  spot gives you an idea of  different level of metabolic activity in  different tissue  now this pet scan can also detect cancer  like cancer cells are glucose hungry  cells because they have a high level of  metabolism as well as very much  increased cellular activity  so as they take up lot amount of glucose  they also take up a lot amount of 18 fdg  and hence they give high density gamma  emissions or a hot spot as you can see  in the image of this pet scan  but my friend the problem is not over  yet you can see a hot spot near the  lungs in the thorax but  but from this image you cannot actually  tell whether the hotspot is in the lungs  or in the heart or in some mediastinal  organ because the quality of this image  or the resolution of this image is quite  low  and based on this imaging only a doctor  cannot comment on the particular  location of the tumor or the cancer  so a doctor needs more  so here the  scientists again brought about a change  that means  they took the paid scan  similarly they took a cd scan now ct  scan is known or mri scan is known for  their high resolution images and they  give you higher level of anatomical or  structural localization  now using proper softwares they  superimposed these two images to get  something known as a pet ct here you get  the metabolic activity along with the  anatomical localization of that  particular metabolic activity so in that  way you can find out a highly metabolic  spot or a hotspot and also you can know  exactly in which anatomical structure or  in which anatomical location your  particular hotspot lies that gear that  gives you an opportunity to localize the  lesion in a particular way  [Music]  so in summary what we learned we learned  that pet scan technique reveals the  metabolic or biochemical functioning of  your tissues and organs  in this technique the key player is the  positron  which is the antimatter counterpart of  electron and the gamma ray emission  which is picked up by the detector by  coincidence imaging  the mechanism of pet scan we learnt in  detail the annihilation reaction  coincidence imaging gamma ray emission  etc  and finally we learned that pet scan can  be used to detect metabolically active  lesions such as cancer  now we also learned how to interpret the  pet scan data based on the two scenarios  that we took up beyond hot spot and cold  spots  now to get notes and flash cards you can  follow the facebook page and instagram  of animated biologies with urban the  link will be in the description  also you can support this channel so  that we can keep on making high quality  content on patreon also you can go for a  super thanks  by clicking on the super thanks button  on the bottom right corner of the video  and you can contribute using paytm  paypal or upi  now if you wish to connect with arpan  you can find his social links in the  description below also for medicine  related content follow me then medic on  youtube  and all make sure you subscribe to this  channel like the video and share this  video among your peers until then bye  bye see you in the next one
 

